Help me review this PR by creating an HTML artifact that describes it. I'm not familiar with the retry/backoff logic so focus on that. Render the actual diff, color-code findings by severity, and annotate the lines they refer to.

The PR changes src/retry.ts:
```diff
 export async function fetchWithRetry(url: string, tries = 3) {
-  for (let i = 0; i < tries; i++) {
-    try { return await fetch(url); } catch (e) { /* ignore */ }
-  }
-  throw new Error('unreachable');
+  let delay = 100;
+  for (let i = 0; i < tries; i++) {
+    try { return await fetch(url); }
+    catch (e) { await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, delay)); delay *= 2; }
+  }
+  return fetch(url); // last attempt surfaces the real error
 }
```
Findings: (high) the old catch swallowed every error making outages invisible — fixed by the final unguarded fetch; (medium) backoff has no jitter, so synchronized clients can thundering-herd; (low) delay is not capped — a long retry chain could wait minutes.
